C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\build-asan            
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 
                                                 



codex
The decoder arms contradict two premises: both UBFX and SBFX can produce width 31, and `1U` makes that width defined. Copying `#510` verbatim into BFI would therefore leave 465 undefined pairs, not 467. I’m checking that the added guard preserves all 556 currently defined pairs, including width zero.
